  "retrieval_hints": [
    "Spec: specs/001-real-time-monitoring/spec.md (FR-001..FR-042). Plan: plan.md. Decisions: research.md (R-001..R-014). Tasks: tasks.md (T001..T124).",
    "Core design rule (R-001): native emits ONLY raw ProbeSample + NetworkStateChange. Every derived value lives in packages/network_analyzer/lib/src/monitoring/. Never add metric maths to Kotlin or Swift.",
    "Defaults: 1s probe interval, 1s probe timeout, 10-sample rolling window. Health: latency 100/250ms, loss 1/5%, jitter 30/50ms, worst-of-three. Spike: >2.0x window mean AND >=50ms above it.",
    "Window-scoped and recovering: packet loss, jitter, health. Cumulative for the session: spike count, uptime, average/lowest/highest latency.",
    "One session at a time. Auto-stop fires only on a 1->0 subscriber transition, so a never-subscribed session keeps running.",
    "stopMonitoring() ends emission; dispose() completes the streams. Documented deviation from the literal wording of FR-016 - see the dartdoc on MonitoringController.dispose.",
    "Pigeon constraints: event-channel methods take no parameters and must all live in one @EventChannelApi; a wire field must not be named 'protocol' (reserved in Swift, emitted unescaped) - hence probeProtocol.",
    "ICMP is IPv4-only; an IPv6-only network returns UnsupportedCapabilityFailure. Upgrade path marked with 'ponytail:' comments at both IcmpProber sites.",
    "iOS gotcha: <net/route.h> is absent from the iOS SDK (rt_msghdr, RTF_*, RTA_* unavailable to Swift AND C), while CTL_NET/PF_ROUTE/NET_RT_DUMP are present in <sys/socket.h>. Verify Swift with `swiftc -typecheck -sdk $(xcrun --sdk iphoneos --show-sdk-path)` \u2014 `-parse` alone resolves no symbols.",
    "Probe semantics learned on-device: TCP refused (RST) = success with timing, on both platforms; Darwin ICMP dgram sockets deliver the IPv4 header (strip before parsing, loop for matching sequence); SO_SNDTIMEO does not bound blocking connect() on Darwin \u2014 iOS TCP uses non-blocking connect + poll + SO_ERROR.",
    "Environment truths (device-validated, documented in quickstart + dartdoc): carriers deprioritize ICMP (high/variable latency on cellular is real); cellular 'gateway' drops probes on most carriers (use internet monitor there); Android emulator slirp NAT forwards no external ICMP and distorts all latency."
  ]
}
